      },
      "worked": "Each trailing zero requires a factor of $10 = 2 \\times 5$. There are more factors of 2 than factors of 5 in $100!$, so count the factors of 5.\n\nAmong the integers from 1 to 100, there are 20 multiples of 5. The four multiples of 25 each contribute an additional factor of 5. There are no multiples of 125.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of factors of }5 &= 20 + 4 \\\\ \\text{Number of factors of }5 &= 24.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $100!$ concludes with 24 zeroes.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
